# ── WoW Forever TOC ──
# SCAFFOLD. This flavor is recognized by Core/Environment.lua and has its own
# profile in Core/Profile.lua, but no researched Data/<Flavor> content yet, so
# this TOC lists the shared Core engine and ErrorLog ONLY. The addon loads,
# reports its own state and captures errors; it gives no advice at all rather
# than applying another expansion's numbers to this one. Add the flavor's
# Data/ and Modules/ files here at the same time its profile stops being a
# scaffold — the TOC is the packaging backstop, the profile the runtime one.
#
# Interface 16001 = the 2026-09 Forever beta (folder _classic_beta_, WowB.exe).
# Forever reports WOW_PROJECT_MAINLINE with a 1.60.x interface: Vanilla-era
# content on Mainline's API. Whether the client actually looks for a
# _Forever suffix is unconfirmed; if it does not, it falls through to
# ToonAge_Mainline.toc / ToonAge.toc, and Core/Profile.lua still gates it
# to the forever profile. Both paths are safe; only the addon-list title
# differs, which is how we will tell which one the client picked.

# ── Libraries ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Libs\LibStub.lua

# ── Core Framework (SHARED — flavor-neutral) ───────────────────────────
Core\Init.lua
Core\Environment.lua
Core\Compat\API.lua
Core\Utils.lua
Core\State.lua
Core\UI.lua
Core\UIModern.lua
Core\MinimapButton.lua
Core\ApiGuard.lua
Core\Profile.lua

# ── Shared infrastructure (no game-rule content) ───────────────────────
Modules\Infrastructure\ErrorLog.lua
